From 4edc8a7637470abaafddd28fc0e96b7aded16fa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:07:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] build: enable neard.service by default

neard.service's [Install] section contains only
Alias=dbus-org.neard.service, which tells systemd what symlink bus
activation may create, not what `systemctl enable` should do. So
`systemctl enable neard` exits 0 and enables nothing: it creates no
multi-user.target.wants symlink, and the service stays disabled -- the
command reports success while leaving the daemon that nothing starts at
boot.

A user who runs the standard enable step to get NFC working at boot sees no
error and no NFC. Add WantedBy=multi-user.target so enabling the unit
actually enables it, independent of whichever bus-activation mechanism ends
up starting it on demand.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 src/neard.service.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/neard.service.in b/src/neard.service.in
index dfa238c..540da7e 100644
--- a/src/neard.service.in
+++ b/src/neard.service.in
@@ -9,4 +9,5 @@ ExecStart=@pkglibexecdir@/neard -n
 LimitNPROC=1
 
 [Install]
+WantedBy=multi-user.target
 Alias=dbus-org.neard.service
-- 
2.55.0

